      "refersTo": "view-switch",
      "description": "Chat and map share one compact control alongside project navigation.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-nav\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"View\"><button aria-pressed=\"false\">Chat</button><button aria-pressed=\"true\">Map</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:32px;padding:2px;background:var(--color-card);border:1px solid var(--color-line);border-radius:var(--radius-control)}.ds-nav button{font-family:var(--font-sans);height:100%;padding:0 12px;border:0;border-radius:var(--radius-tag);background:transparent;color:var(--color-ink-muted);font-size:.875rem;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color .15s ease}.ds-nav button[aria-pressed=false]:hover{background:var(--color-wash);color:var(--color-ink)}.ds-nav button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--color-ink);color:var(--color-card);cursor:default}.ds-primary:focus-visible,.ds-secondary:focus-visible,.ds-nav button:focus-visible,.ds-tag:focus-visible,.ds-file-name:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Provenance tag",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "provenance-tag",
      "description": "A compact action linking a derived node to its sources.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-tag\">Sources · 3</button>",
      "css": ".ds-tag{font-family:var(--font-sans);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:2px 6px;border:0;border-radius:var(--radius-tag);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-accent) 10%,transparent);color:var(--color-accent);font-size:.8125rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.35;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color .15s ease}.ds-tag:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-accent) 20%,transparent)}.ds-primary:focus-visible,.ds-secondary:focus-visible,.ds-nav button:focus-visible,.ds-tag:focus-visible,.ds-file-name:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Start node",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "thought-node",
      "description": "A representative start card with its accent integrated into the continuous border.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-start\"><header><button aria-label=\"Collapse\">⌄</button><span>Start</span></header><div class=\"ds-node-body\">What should this conversation explore?</div></article>",
      "css": ".ds-start{font-family:var(--font-sans);width:520px;max-width:100%;background:var(--color-card);color:var(--color-ink);border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-accent) 30%,var(--color-line));border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);border-radius:var(--radius-node);box-shadow:none;transition:border-color .16s ease}.ds-start:hover{border-color:var(--color-line-strong);border-left-color:var(--color-accent)}.ds-start header{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:8px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line)}.ds-start header button{width:28px;height:28px;border:0;border-radius:var(--radius-control);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-accent) 10%,transparent);color:var(--color-accent);cursor:pointer}.ds-start header button:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-accent) 15%,transparent)}.ds-start header button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}.ds-start header span{font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--color-accent-strong)}.ds-node-body{padding:16px 20px;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;overflow-wrap:anywhere}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Note material",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "note-node",
      "description": "Warm paper distinguishes source notes from generated responses.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-note\"><header>Note</header><div>Research observations and source text.</div></article>",
      "css": ".ds-note{font-family:var(--font-sans);background:var(--color-material-note);color:var(--color-ink);border:1px solid var(--color-material-note-line);border-radius:var(--radius-node);box-shadow:none}.ds-note header{padding:12px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-material-note-line);color:var(--color-material-note-ink);font-size:.875rem;font-weight:500}.ds-note>div{padding:16px 20px;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.85;overflow-wrap:anywhere}"
    },
    {
      "name": "File material",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "file-node",
      "description": "Filename-derived extension identity, source name, and an illustrative byte-size label.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-file\"><header>Files</header><div class=\"ds-file-row\"><span class=\"ds-file-identity\"><svg width=\"21\" height=\"21\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8Z\"/><path d=\"M14 2v6h6M8 13h8M8 17h6\"/></svg><span>.docx</span></span><div><button class=\"ds-file-name\">Research notes.docx</button><div class=\"ds-file-meta\">24.0 KiB</div></div></div></article>",
      "css": ".ds-file{font-family:var(--font-sans);background:var(--color-card);color:var(--color-ink);border:1px solid var(--color-material-file-line);border-radius:var(--radius-node);box-shadow:none}.ds-file header{padding:12px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line);color:var(--color-material-file-ink);font-size:.875rem;font-weight:500}.ds-file-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:12px 16px}.ds-file-identity{flex:0 0 58px;min-height:64px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:5px;border:1px solid var(--color-material-file-line);border-radius:var(--radius-control);color:var(--color-material-file-ink);background:var(--color-material-file-wash)}.ds-file-identity span{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;line-height:1.2}.ds-file-name{font-family:var(--font-sans);background:transparent;color:var(--color-ink);border:0;padding:0;font-size:15px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;overflow-wrap:anywhere;cursor:pointer}.ds-file-name:hover{color:var(--color-accent)}.ds-file-meta{margin-top:5px;color:var(--color-ink-faint);font-size:12px}.ds-primary:focus-visible,.ds-secondary:focus-visible,.ds-nav button:focus-visible,.ds-tag:focus-visible,.ds-file-name:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Continuous reading panel",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "focus-panel",
      "description": "A bounded overlay whose internal sections share one reading surface.",
      "html": "<aside class=\"ds-panel\"><header>Conversation</header><section><strong>Question</strong><p>What does this source establish?</p></section><section><strong>Response</strong><p>The reading region remains continuous between sections.</p></section></aside>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:var(--font-sans);width:520px;max-width:100%;background:var(--color-card);color:var(--color-ink);border:1px solid var(--color-line);border-radius:var(--radius-panel);box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg);overflow:hidden}.ds-panel header{padding:8px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line);font-size:.875rem}.ds-panel section{margin:0;padding:12px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-line);background:transparent;border-radius:0;box-shadow:none;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7}.ds-panel section:last-child{border-bottom:0}.ds-panel strong{font-weight:600}.ds-panel p{margin:8px 0 0}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "overview": "ThoughtDAG is an editable conversation canvas: readable question-and-answer cards, directional context edges, and a continuous reading panel. Cool neutral surfaces keep graph structure legible; purple identifies the main conversation and orange identifies exploration.\n\nThis documents the implemented visual system, not a completed accessibility audit or a claim that every detail was individually approved. Rounded corners are welcome when outlines, dividers, and accents join coherently.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Stable graph geometry across interaction and appearance.",
      "Compact controls, readable content, and restrained overlay depth.",
      "Distinct start, note, and file identities at every semantic zoom tier."
    ],
    "rules": [
      "Editing and dismissal: reversible short names commit outside; content editors suspend with session drafts, including empty drafts. Escape cancels only the top layer; sending, generation, authorization, deletion, and configuration submission require explicit action. See docs/reference/interaction-contract.md and reuse the shared dismiss hooks.",
      "Canvas spacing: 16px viewport and content insets, 8px toolbar padding, 4px control gaps, 32px controls, 12px section spacing. Compact overview names use 8px padding with the same zoom compensation as their text. Top control groups wrap in the visible canvas.",
      "Node proportions: 28px header controls with 8px vertical padding; 12px working ports and 16px overview ports; 18px corner grips follow canvas zoom while their invisible hit areas remain generous. Arrowheads use canvas coordinates independently of stroke thickness. First-question inputs group 16px search and send icons in a padded composer with 32px actions."
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the semantic radius tokens and a continuous card outline.",
      "Do preserve context-arrow order and vertical alignment within each conversation chain.",
      "Do keep top-left project and session controls aligned at the same height.",
      "Do retain node names and file extensions when reducing visual detail.",
      "Do use actual filenames, extensions, and available file sizes.",
      "Do verify light and dark appearances without changing component geometry."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace coherent rounded corners with an all-square interface.",
      "Don't add a detached decorative stripe that breaks a card's outline.",
      "Don't translate nodes on hover or clip their external connection ports.",
      "Don't add stacked shadows to the minimap or turn its viewport mask into a dark slab.",
      "Don't nest raised cards throughout the focus panel's reading area.",
      "Don't invent file metadata, previews, or promotional third-party UI copy."
    ]
  }
}
